 We are seeking the sharpest minds to take our world-class Subsea Production Control System technology even further. To meet new challenges and opportunities we are seeking a determined and motivated Cybersecurity & DevOps Engineer to join our SW Team in Controls and Automation.
What you’ll do
In your job you will be responsible for implementing DevOps practices across SW Teams, establishing CI/CD systems, creating, managing, measuring and improving the processes and pipelines. 
Responsible for activities related to AWS, GitHub, Atlassian Admin, such as user access security and control, cost optimization, creating new features and virtual setups, and supporting microservices architecture.
What we’re looking for
Knowledge of AWS, GitHub, Atlassian (Jira/Confluence);
Very good understanding of DevOps principles (Three Ways, CALMS);
Good knowledge of AWS cloud, including technologies like: EC2, ASG, VPC, ECS, EKS, S3
Knowledge of Monitoring and Observability tools and practices (AWS X-Ray, CloudWatch, Grafana, logs and alarms);
Experience in (cloud) development, monitoring and optimizing cloud costs;
Experience with automation and Infrastructure as Code, using Terraform, cloudformation, AWS cdk;
Experience with virtualization, images creation, and use of custom builds of OS for virtualized environments; 
Experience with Managing cloud servers Supporting Linux/Windows machines;
Experience with defining and implementing CI/CD Pipelines standards and security best practices, to improve software deployment lead time and quality;
Experience with defining and implementing standards for containerization using Kubernetes, including comparison between suppliers (RedHat/SUSE) on premise and on cloud.
 
 
#LI-AM5

